{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791388515,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_20261007235510d345d0ef4c344eee\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: outline(name), read_method(name, method, class), write_method(name, method, source - one METHOD block, class), read_object(name, include main|testclasses), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: prefer outline, read_method and write_method for changing existing methods; use write_source only for new methods, changed declarations or a new test include, and then write the FULL source; read before write; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG (settings from pia.env), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"TheLet me start by reading the config class ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG which reads pia.env settings.\\n\\nThe bug: value parsing doesn't strip trailing comments (e.g., \\\"glm-5.3 # optional\\\"). Also the turn mode setting being ignored might be because \\\"job # optional: job | daemon | inline\\\" doesn't match 'job', so it falls back to default inline maybe.\\n\\nLet me read the class and its test classes.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_20261007235510d345d0ef4c344eee\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7227987921133892991\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7227987921133892991\",\"name\":\"read_object\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7227987921133892990\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7227987921133892990\",\"name\":\"outline\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1361,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":1216},\"output_tokens\":124,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":91},\"total_tokens\":1485}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791388560,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_202610072355155b4ddc17dc954ef3\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: outline(name), read_method(name, method, class), write_method(name, method, source - one METHOD block, class), read_object(name, include main|testclasses), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: prefer outline, read_method and write_method for changing existing methods; use write_source only for new methods, changed declarations or a new test include, and then write the FULL source; read before write; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG (settings from pia.env), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The bug: `get_from` reads the value after `=` without stripping inline comments (` # comment`) or surrounding blanks. So `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` yields `glm-5.3 # optional`.\\n\\nAlso note: no trimming of whitespace around key and value. And no handling of comment lines starting with `#` \u2014 those don't contain `=` typically, so they're skipped; but a comment line like `# PIA_MODEL=foo` would match the key! That's a secondary bug: a full-line comment `# PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3` would return `glm-5.3`. We should skip lines starting with `#` (after leading blanks).\\n\\nAlso turn mode setting ignored: because value is `job # optional: job | daemon | inline` and the executor probably compares with `job`, `daemon`, `inline` strictly, so it falls to default. Actually \\\"ignored\\\" means it isn't recognized, default used.\\n\\nLet me look at how the executor reads PIA_TURN_MODE to write a test there too. Let me check ZCL_PIA_30_* terminal/turns.\\n\\nFirst, let me write a failing test in ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG's testclasses include. But testclasses include may not exist yet \u2014 outline only lists main methods. Let me try reading testclasses to see.\\n\\nThe test needs to create a pia.env file to read. That could be dangerous in a real system (writing files on app server). Better: refactor so the parsing logic is testable without file I/O \u2014 e.g. extract a static method `parse_value( iv_line )` or make `get_from` accept... Actually a cleaner approach: add a private static method `value_of_line` that parses a line, and test it. But TDD asks for a red test reproducing the bug. A test of the parsing method reproduces the bug at the unit level. Also can test full-file behavior by writing a temp file \u2014 but writing files in unit tests on an app server is risky; the class itself only reads `pia.env`. I could add a test that writes a temp file via DATASET... but ABAP Unit tests shouldn't create files. I'll test via a new pure parsing method. Actually, to keep the red test honest, I can write the test against a new method `parse` \u2014 but then the test wouldn't compile before the method exists (red = failing, not syntax error). Standard approach: first add the method with buggy behavior? Hmm.\\n\\nAlternative: test the file path with a test file. `get_from` takes iv_file \u2014 it's private but tests in the local test class can access private static methods (local classes of the same class-includes can access private components? Yes \u2014 local test classes in the testclasses include of a global class can access its private components, since they're in the same \\\"friend\\\"/program context. Actually local classes defined in the testclass include of the class are implicitly friends of the class? By default, ABAP Unit test classes have access to private components of the class under test when included via the CLASS-LOCAL TEST ... yes: test classes included in the class's testclasses include can access private components (they are part of the same program and the class under test is implicitly \\\"PRIVATE ACCESS\\\" via the local friend definition: \\\"CLASS lcl_test DEFINITION ... FOR TESTING\\\" within the same include grants access because global class grants friendship to local test classes automatically). Correct: local classes in a global class's test include are friends of the global class, so private methods accessible.\\n\\nSo the test could write a temp file `pia_test.env` in DIR_HOME via OPEN DATASET FOR OUTPUT, then call get_from. Writing a file in unit tests is acceptable-ish for a sandbox; risk: file remains. Many PIA-style systems allow this. But cleaner and safer: test via a pure function.\\n\\nPlan:\\n1. Add a private static method `parse_line( iv_line ) RETURNING VALUE(rv_val) ...` plus key check. Actually simplest: add method `value_of( iv_line TYPE string iv_name TYPE string ) RETURNING rv_` that does line-level parsing without file I/O, and `get_from` delegates to it. Then tests call `value_of`. To have a red test first, I need the method to exist with the buggy behavior before the fix... The instructions: \\\"write an ABAP Unit test that reproduces it and is red, then fix the code\\\". A pragmatic route: write the test include with tests against `get_from` with a real temp file \u2014 red with current code \u2014 then fix. The file approach truly reproduces end-to-end. I'll do both: write test include with tests using a temp file (created in test setup, deleted in teardown), calling private `get_from`. Red. Then fix `get_from` (strip inline comment, trim blanks, skip full-line comments) and show green.\\n\\nFile path: use `pia.env`? No \u2014 don't clobber the admin's real file! Use `pia_test.env`. get_from accepts iv_file.\\n\\nAlso test PIA_TURN_MODE ignoring: where is turn mode read? Let me check ZCL_PIA_30_* for usage, to mention cause. Let me grep... I can't grep; let me outline ZCL_PIA_30_TURN or read. Let me check quickly: outline zcl_pia_30_terminal? The rules say ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Let me outline a couple to find where PIA_TURN_MODE is read.\\n\\nActually the root cause is fully in ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG: value contains trailing \\\" # optional...\\\" so downstream comparisons fail. The fix in config suffices. But to demonstrate \\\"turn mode setting is ignored\\\" is fixed, a unit test on get_from/get for PIA_TURN_MODE returning `job` is enough. Let me still check the consumer to confirm it does exact compare (so my explanation is accurate).\\n\\nLet me write the test include. Careful: writing files in ABAP Unit on app server \u2014 OPEN DATASET ... FOR OUTPUT in a sandbox with OSD_DATASET_HOME. Should work.\\n\\nTest cases:\\n1. `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` -\\u003e expect `glm-5.3` (red: actual `glm-5.3 # optional`).\\n2. `PIA_TURN_MODE=job # optional: job | daemon | inline` -\\u003e expect `job`.\\n3. Comment line `# PIA_MODEL=other` should be ignored; real line later wins.\\n4. Blanks: `PIA_LLM = z.ai ` -\\u003e expect `z.ai` (trim).\\n5. No comment when `#` inside value? Keep simple: cut at first ` #` (space-hash) \u2014 README-style. I'll strip everything from the first `#` that is preceded by a space or at value start? Safer common convention: treat `#` after whitespace as comment start. For URLs there's no `#` typically. I'll implement: find first occurrence of `#` in the value part; if found, truncate there; then trim blanks/tabs. Also if value empty after trim -\\u003e keep empty (fall through to c_settings). Also skip lines whose trimmed form starts with `#`.\\n\\nAlso trim key of blanks? `PIA_MODEL =glm` \u2192 key `PIA_MODEL ` mismatch. Trim key too \u2014 good robustness. Keep test list focused.\\n\\nNow write the testclasses include. Format like:\\n\\nCLASS ltcl_config DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\n  DURATION SHORT RISK LEVEL HARMLESS.\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\n    CONSTANTS c_test_file TYPE string VALUE `pia_test.env`.\\n    CLASS-METHODS write_env IMPORTING iv_content TYPE string.\\n    METHODS teardown.\\n    METHODS model_with_inline_comment FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\n    METHODS turn_mode_with_inline_comment FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\n    METHODS full_line_comment_ignored FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\n    METHODS blanks_around_value FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\nENDCLASS.\\n\\nImplementation uses cl_abap_unit_assert.\\n\\nwrite_env: CONCATENATE lines with |\\\\n| into string xstring? WRITE DATASET writes string in text mode; use string with newline. Build string with lines joined by cl_abap_char_utilities=\\u003enewline. Write it with TRANSFER... In TEXT MODE, TRANSFER of a string containing \\\\n \u2014 newline char (0A) is written as-is in text mode? In text mode, the end-of-line marker for non-Unix servers gets converted, and embedded newlines in the string can cause issues. Safer: split content into lines table and TRANSFER each line separately.\\n\\nCLASS-METHODS write_env:\\n  DATA lt_lines TYPE string_table.\\n  SPLIT iv_content AT |\\\\n| INTO TABLE lt_lines. -- need to filter empty? If content ends with \\\\n, last empty line \u2014 TRANSFER empty line writes empty line, fine.\\n  OPEN DATASET c_test_file FOR OUTPUT IN TEXT MODE ENCODING UTF-8.\\n  LOOP AT lt_lines INTO DATA(lv_line). TRANSFER lv_line. ENDLOOP. CLOSE DATASET.\\n\\nteardown: DELETE DATASET c_test_file. IGNORE.\\n\\nAssertions: zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from( iv_file = c_test_file iv_name = 'PIA_MODEL' ) \u2014 private but accessible from local test class (friend). Yes.\\n\\nNow, run_tests must be on published active code. Sequence: first write testclasses include, activate, run tests \u2192 red. Then fix get_from, activate, run tests \u2192 green.\\n\\nLet me also check the turn-mode consumer for explanation accuracy. I'll outline ZCL_PIA_30_TURN... I don't know exact names. The prompt says ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). I'll skip deep reading but maybe quick outline of one. Actually to be accurate in final answer I can just state the mechanism generically. But better verify quickly with an outline \u2014 cheap. I'll do outline on zcl_pia_30_terminal? I'd rather not guess names and waste calls; skip. The cause is fully in config.\\n\\nLet me write the test include now.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_202610072355155b4ddc17dc954ef3\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"text\":\"I'll start by reading the config class (done above). The cause is visible in `GET_FROM`: the value is everything after `=`, with no trimming and no handling of `#` comments \u2014 so `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` yields `glm-5.3 # optional`, and `PIA_TURN_MODE=job # ...` no longer matches `job`/`daemon`/`inline` downstream.\\n\\nLet me write a red unit test against the existing behavior (via a temp file, calling the private `GET_FROM`, which local test classes may access).\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_202610072355155b4ddc17dc954ef3\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"testclasses\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS ltcl_config DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\\\n  DURATION SHORT RISK LEVEL HARMLESS.\\\\n\\\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\\\n    CONSTANTS c_test_file TYPE string VALUE `pia_test.env`.\\\\n\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS write_env\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_content TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    METHODS teardown.\\\\n    METHODS inline_comment_on_model FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS inline_comment_on_turn_mode FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS full_line_comment_ignored FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS blanks_around_value_trimmed FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS value_without_comment_untouched FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS ltcl_config IMPLEMENTATION.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD write_env.\\\\n    DATA lt_lines TYPE STANDARD TABLE OF string WITH DEFAULT KEY.\\\\n\\\\n    SPLIT iv_content AT |\\\\\\\\n| INTO TABLE lt_lines.\\\\n    OPEN DATASET c_test_file FOR OUTPUT IN TEXT MODE ENCODING UTF-8.\\\\n    LOOP AT lt_lines INTO DATA(lv_line).\\\\n      TRANSFER lv_line TO c_test_file.\\\\n    ENDLOOP.\\\\n    CLOSE DATASET c_test_file.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD teardown.\\\\n    TRY.\\\\n        DELETE DATASET c_test_file.\\\\n      CATCH cx_root ##NO_HANDLER.\\\\n    ENDTRY.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD inline_comment_on_model.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" README-style line: value followed by a comment\\\\n    write_env( `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `glm-5.3`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_MODEL` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD inline_comment_on_turn_mode.\\\\n    write_env( `PIA_TURN_MODE=job # optional: job | daemon | inline` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `job`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_TURN_MODE` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD full_line_comment_ignored.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" a commented-out line must not win over the real one\\\\n    write_env( |# PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash\\\\\\\\nPIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional| ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `glm-5.3`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_MODEL` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD blanks_around_value_trimmed.\\\\n    write_env( `PIA_LLM = z.ai ` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `z.ai`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_LLM` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD value_without_comment_untouched.\\\\n    write_env( `PIA_LLM=z.ai` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `z.ai`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_LLM` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7227991631985633304\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7227991631985633304\",\"name\":\"write_source\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2029,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":1344},\"output_tokens\":2975,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":2114},\"total_tokens\":5004}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791388567,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_202610072356017676ee32f40e47f1\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: outline(name), read_method(name, method, class), write_method(name, method, source - one METHOD block, class), read_object(name, include main|testclasses), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: prefer outline, read_method and write_method for changing existing methods; use write_source only for new methods, changed declarations or a new test include, and then write the FULL source; read before write; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG (settings from pia.env), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Now activate and run tests to see them red. But the tests would currently be red only for comment tests; blanks test also red. Note: get_from is private; test class is local in the same include \u2014 local test classes can access private methods of the class under test? Yes, ABAP Unit local test classes in the testclasses include of a class are friends of the class under test by default (the compiler implicitly adds \\\"LOCAL FRIENDS\\\"). Yes \u2014 the class under test grants friendship to local test classes automatically.\\n\\nActivate then run tests.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_202610072356017676ee32f40e47f1\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228003623534323305\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228003623534323305\",\"name\":\"activate\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2798,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":1216},\"output_tokens\":127,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":110},\"total_tokens\":2925}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791388595,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_20261007235621a133af0609994730\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: outline(name), read_method(name, method, class), write_method(name, method, source - one METHOD block, class), read_object(name, include main|testclasses), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: prefer outline, read_method and write_method for changing existing methods; use write_source only for new methods, changed declarations or a new test include, and then write the FULL source; read before write; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG (settings from pia.env), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Two issues:\\n1. Method name too long \u2014 rename.\\n2. get_from is private. Tests are in the local testclass include; local test classes CAN access private methods if they are declared as FOR TESTING and the class under test... no \u2014 friendship needed. Actually in ABAP, local test classes in the testclasses include of a class are implicitly friends of the class under test? No \u2014 the rule is: the local test classes are friends of the class under test ONLY if declared via \\\"LOCAL FRIENDS\\\". In class includes, you write `CLASS ltcl_x DEFINITION ... .` and you can add `CLASS zcl_pia_00_config LOCAL FRIENDS ltcl_x.` in the testclasses include. Yes, that's the standard mechanism.\\n\\nSo add `CLASS zcl_pia_00_config DEFINITION LOCAL FRIENDS ltcl_config.` before the test class definition.\\n\\nAlternatively test via get() with a seam, but get() reads c_file / c_settings, which I can't redirect without changing main code. Using LOCAL FRIENDS is cleaner and lets me test get_from directly.\\n\\nFix both, rewrite testclasses include, then write the fix to get_from, activate once, run tests. But wait \u2014 the task says: write a red test first, show red, then fix, then green. To run tests red I'd need to activate the test include with the unfixed main code. So: activate testclasses with local friends + short name, run tests \u2192 red. Then fix get_from via write_method, activate, run tests \u2192 green.\\n\\nRename value_without_comment_untouched \u2192 value_without_comment.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_20261007235621a133af0609994730\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"text\":\"Two fixes needed: a shorter method name and `LOCAL FRIENDS` so the test can call the private `get_from`.\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_20261007235621a133af0609994730\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"testclasses\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS zcl_pia_00_config DEFINITION LOCAL FRIENDS ltcl_config.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS ltcl_config DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\\\n  DURATION SHORT RISK LEVEL HARMLESS.\\\\n\\\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\\\n    CONSTANTS c_test_file TYPE string VALUE `pia_test.env`.\\\\n\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS write_env\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_content TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    METHODS teardown.\\\\n    METHODS inline_comment_on_model FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS inline_comment_on_turn_mode FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS full_line_comment_ignored FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS blanks_around_value_trimmed FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS value_without_comment FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS ltcl_config IMPLEMENTATION.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD write_env.\\\\n    DATA lt_lines TYPE STANDARD TABLE OF string WITH DEFAULT KEY.\\\\n\\\\n    SPLIT iv_content AT |\\\\\\\\n| INTO TABLE lt_lines.\\\\n    OPEN DATASET c_test_file FOR OUTPUT IN TEXT MODE ENCODING UTF-8.\\\\n    LOOP AT lt_lines INTO DATA(lv_line).\\\\n      TRANSFER lv_line TO c_test_file.\\\\n    ENDLOOP.\\\\n    CLOSE DATASET c_test_file.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD teardown.\\\\n    TRY.\\\\n        DELETE DATASET c_test_file.\\\\n      CATCH cx_root ##NO_HANDLER.\\\\n    ENDTRY.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD inline_comment_on_model.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" README-style line: value followed by a comment\\\\n    write_env( `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `glm-5.3`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_MODEL` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD inline_comment_on_turn_mode.\\\\n    write_env( `PIA_TURN_MODE=job # optional: job | daemon | inline` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `job`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_TURN_MODE` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD full_line_comment_ignored.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" a commented-out line must not win over the real one\\\\n    write_env( |# PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash\\\\\\\\nPIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional| ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `glm-5.3`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_MODEL` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD blanks_around_value_trimmed.\\\\n    write_env( `PIA_LLM = z.ai ` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `z.ai`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_LLM` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD value_without_comment.\\\\n    write_env( `PIA_LLM=z.ai` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `z.ai`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_LLM` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7227991460186943063\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7227991460186943063\",\"name\":\"write_source\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":3207,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":1984},\"output_tokens\":1104,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":330},\"total_tokens\":4311}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791388597,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_20261007235635d8435721d74046ac\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: outline(name), read_method(name, method, class), write_method(name, method, source - one METHOD block, class), read_object(name, include main|testclasses), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: prefer outline, read_method and write_method for changing existing methods; use write_source only for new methods, changed declarations or a new test include, and then write the FULL source; read before write; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG (settings from pia.env), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7227998194695664299\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7227998194695664299\",\"name\":\"activate\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":3987,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":2752},\"output_tokens\":17,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":0},\"total_tokens\":4004}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791388664,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_202610072356491b90b338d7954af3\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: outline(name), read_method(name, method, class), write_method(name, method, source - one METHOD block, class), read_object(name, include main|testclasses), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: prefer outline, read_method and write_method for changing existing methods; use write_source only for new methods, changed declarations or a new test include, and then write the FULL source; read before write; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG (settings from pia.env), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The LOCAL FRIENDS statement must come after the class definition of ltcl_config, not before. Actually in the testclasses include, the standard pattern is:\\n\\n```abap\\nCLASS ltcl_config DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING ...\\n  ...\\nENDCLASS.\\n\\nCLASS zcl_pia_00_config DEFINITION LOCAL FRIENDS ltcl_config.\\n```\\n\\nWait, no. The friend declaration must be in the class definition of the granting class or... Actually for local test classes in the testclasses include of a global class, the standard is:\\n\\nThe testclasses include is included in the class pool after the local classes of the main include. The statement `CLASS zcl_pia_00_config DEFINITION LOCAL FRIENDS ltcl_x.` must appear in the test include, but it's a forward declaration granting friendship. It can appear anywhere in the test include \u2014 but the error \\\"Class LTCL_CONFIG not found\\\" at line 1 col 1... hmm, that's because at line 1 the class ltcl_config is not yet known? Actually LOCAL FRIENDS with a not-yet-defined class should be fine (forward declaration). But the checker complains.\\n\\nHmm, the error might be because the friends statement must come AFTER the definition of the local class in the file order for this checker. Let me place the friends statement after ENDCLASS of ltcl_config definition.\\n\\nActually the standard pattern from SAP examples:\\n\\n```abap\\nCLASS ltcl_test DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\n  DURATION SHORT RISK LEVEL HARMLESS.\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\n    ...\\nENDCLASS.\\n\\nCLASS ltcl_test IMPLEMENTATION.\\n  ...\\nENDCLASS.\\n```\\n\\nAnd friendship for private methods of the global class: local classes in the testclasses include are implicitly friends of the global class? Yes! Actually the local test classes in the test class include are implicitly friends of the global class whose pool they belong to. Wait \u2014 the rule: \\\"The classes of the test class include are friends of the global class\\\" \u2014 hmm, actually the local classes in a class pool are friends of the global class automatically? Let me recall: In a class pool, all local classes are friends of the global class? No \u2014 the friendship must be declared... Actually: \\\"In class pools, the local classes and the test classes are implicitly friends of the global class\\\" \u2014 I don't think that's correct in general. Let me recall ABAP documentation: \\\"The classes and interfaces of the test class include are part of the class pool... Test classes have a friendship with the class of the class pool\\\"? Hmm.\\n\\nFrom ABAP docs (ABAP Unit): \\\"A test class defined in the test include of a class pool automatically becomes a friend of the global class of that pool.\\\" I believe this IS true \u2014 test classes in the test include are implicit friends of the global class. Yes: \\\"Test classes in the test class include of a program are automatically friends of the topmost class of the compilation unit\\\" \u2014 something like that. But the checker here complained about private access, meaning either the implicit friendship doesn't apply, or the checker doesn't know.\\n\\nActually the documented rule: test classes in a test include are friends of the classes of the compilation unit in which they're included (for class pools: the global class and local classes). Hmm, but the syntax check says private access is not allowed. Wait \u2014 maybe the issue is that the file is compiled standalone by this environment's checker (it lists FILE .../testclasses.abap), so friendship resolution differs.\\n\\nThe error at line 1 \\\"Class LTCL_CONFIG not found\\\" suggests the checker compiles the file separately and doesn't recognize the forward declaration. Let me instead avoid private access: rather than testing get_from, test via the public get( )? But get( ) reads from c_file = `pia.env` fixed, not injectable. Hmm.\\n\\nAlternative approach: make the parsing logic testable \u2014 e.g., refactor get_from to call a pure static helper `strip_value( iv_line )` \u2014 but same problem: private.\\n\\nOptions:\\n1. Put the parsing in a new public method or a separate helper class (e.g., add a public static method `parse_line` or make `get_from` public for testing). Simplest robust approach within this environment: change GET_FROM to PUBLIC SECTION (visible for testing), or add a public class-method `value_of( iv_line )`.\\n2. Or test via the real file names \u2014 no, would touch the real pia.env; too risky and order-dependent.\\n\\nGiven the environment's checker, the cleanest: make the line-parsing logic a public static method of ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG, e.g. `split_line` / `parse`. Then get_from uses it, and tests call it with strings directly \u2014 no file I/O, no friendship needed. That's better design anyway (pure function, easy to test).\\n\\nLet me restructure:\\n\\nPUBLIC SECTION:\\n- get, model (as before)\\n- class-methods value_of importing iv_line returning rv_value (parses \\\"KEY=VALUE # comment\\\" -\\u003e value trimmed). Hmm but need to return key too for get_from to compare. Maybe two helpers: `strip_comment( iv_line )` returning line without comment, then get_from splits at =, compares key (also trimmed), takes value, condenses.\\n\\nI'll add a public method `clean_line( iv_line ) TYPE string` that removes an inline comment (# ... end) and condenses/trims. get_from uses it before finding '='. Keys with blanks around \u2192 also trim key? My test blanks_around_value_trimmed uses `PIA_LLM = z.ai ` and expects key `PIA_LLM` to match iv_name. If I just CONDENSE the whole line (removes leading/trailing blanks and collapses inner blanks to single), then `PIA_LLM = z.ai ` becomes `PIA_LLM = z.ai` and splitting at '=' gives key `PIA_LLM ` (with trailing blank). Hmm, so I should trim key too. Let me do CONDENSE on the key after substring. Also lowercase? Keep exact match; fine.\\n\\nImplementation for clean_line:\\n```abap\\nMETHOD clean_line.\\n  rv_ = iv_line.\\n  \\\" full-line comments\\n  IF rv_ IS INITIAL.\\n    RETURN.\\n  ENDIF.\\n  \\\" cut everything from the first '#' to the end\\n  FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF `#` IN rv_ MATCH OFFSET DATA(lv_off).\\n  IF sy-subrc = 0.\\n    rv_ = substring( val = rv_ len = lv_off ).\\n  ENDIF.\\n  CONDENSE rv_.\\nENDMETHOD.\\n```\\n\\nCareful: '#' could appear inside a value? For secrets/URLs, '#' in a value is unlikely; README comments use '#'. Acceptable \u2014 and it's exactly what the bug report asks for. But what about a full-line comment `# PIA_MODEL=...`: after cutting at '#', rv_ is empty \u2192 key compare fails, line skipped. Good. But wait: with the existing get_from logic, an empty line \u2192 FIND '=' fails \u2192 CONTINUE. Good.\\n\\nBut careful with ordering in get_from: currently it finds '=' in the raw line. I'll clean first, then find '='.\\n\\nAlso `CONDENSE rv_` collapses inner multiple blanks; for key matching I trim key with SHIFT/CONDENSE: after substring, `CONDENSE lv_key.` \u2014 that removes leading/trailing blanks. Key `PIA_LLM ` \u2192 `PIA_LLM`. Value ` z.ai` \u2192 CONDENSE rv_ after substring? I'll do `CONDENSE rv_.` on the value too. Actually if I CONDENSE the whole cleaned line first, value substring may still start with a blank after '='. So condense value separately.\\n\\nAlso should values keep internal spacing? Values are single tokens (names, URLs); CONDENSE keeps single internal blanks. Fine.\\n\\nNow tests: call public `clean_line`-style method? Better to test observable behavior closest to the bug: I'll expose the parsing via a public method `value_of( iv_name, iv_line )`? Hmm, simpler: keep tests on the private get_from via file I/O but that failed to compile. So instead:\\n\\nPublic method: `class-methods parse_value importing iv_line type string iv_name type string returning value(rv_) type string` \u2014 parses one line, returns value if key matches, else initial. get_from loops lines calling parse_value. Tests then test parse_value directly with strings \u2014 red on old code (old code has no parse_value...). Hmm, TDD red test must fail on current code, not compile error. If I add a new method, the test can't be red on old code because it wouldn't compile.\\n\\nBetter: keep tests targeting existing public surface. The only public methods: get( iv_name ) and model( ). get reads c_file = `pia.env` (constant) then c_settings. Can't inject.\\n\\nAlternative: make GET_FROM public? That changes existing method visibility \u2014 allowed via write_source. Then test calls get_from with iv_file = test file. The red test would compile against old code only if get_from is already public at test time... but the first activation must succeed with the red test. Chicken-and-egg: activation compiles the whole class including tests; if I make get_from public in the same activation as the test, the test would run against the NEW (unfixed) get_from code \u2014 old body, new visibility. That works! The bug is in the body, not visibility. So:\\n\\nStep 1: write_source main with GET_FROM moved to PUBLIC SECTION, body unchanged (still buggy). Write testclasses include calling get_from. Activate \u2192 red tests for comment cases (turn_mode, model with comment, full_line_comment? no that passes on old code? Let's check: old code with `# PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash` line: FIND '=' succeeds, key = `# PIA_MODEL` \u2260 PIA_MODEL \u2192 continue; then `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` \u2192 key matches, value = `glm-5.3 # optional` \u2192 fails expected glm-5.3. Good red). blanks_around_value_trimmed: old code: key = `PIA_LLM ` \u2260 `PIA_LLM` \u2192 no match \u2192 returns initial \u2192 red too. value_without_comment passes.\\nStep 2: run tests \u2192 expect failures (red). \\nStep 3: fix get_from body via write_method.\\nStep 4: activate, run tests \u2192 green.\\n\\nBut hmm \u2014 is making get_from public acceptable design-wise? It was private. For testability in this environment, that's pragmatic. Alternatively add a new public helper `strip_comment`. Both fine. I'll go with making get_from public? It exposes a file-reading method publicly... Alternatively name it as is. I think it's acceptable; note it's for testing.\\n\\nActually cleaner: keep get_from private, and instead test through a new public pure helper? New method = new declaration = test can't be red against old code (compile). Unless I add the helper AND write tests that exercise the old path via get_from... circular.\\n\\nSimplest and honest: make get_from public (comment: public for ABAP Unit tests). Then red \u2192 fix \u2192 green.\\n\\nLet me write main source with get_from in public section, body identical (buggy).\\n\\nThen testclasses without LOCAL FRIENDS.\\n\\nThen activate \u2192 should succeed (syntax ok). Then run_tests \u2192 red on 3 tests (model comment, turn_mode comment, blanks). Note run_tests runs on published/active code \u2014 fine.\\n\\nThen write_method get_from fixed. activate. run_tests \u2192 green.\\n\\nFixed get_from:\\n\\n```abap\\nMETHOD get_from.\\n  DATA lv_line TYPE string.\\n  DATA lv_key TYPE string.\\n  DATA lv_off TYPE i.\\n  DATA lv_from TYPE i.\\n\\n  TRY.\\n      OPEN DATASET iv_file FOR INPUT IN TEXT MODE ENCODING UTF-8.\\n      IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\n        RETURN.\\n      ENDIF.\\n      DO.\\n        READ DATASET iv_file INTO lv_line.\\n        IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\n          EXIT.\\n        ENDIF.\\n        \\\" README style: NAME=value # comment -\\u003e strip the comment\\n        FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF `#` IN lv_line MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\n        IF sy-subrc = 0.\\n          lv_line = substring( val = lv_line len = lv_off ).\\n        ENDIF.\\n        CONDENSE lv_line.\\n        CLEAR lv_off.\\n        FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF `=` IN lv_line MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\n        IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\n          CONTINUE.\\n        ENDIF.\\n        lv_key = substring( val = lv_line len = lv_off ).\\n        CONDENSE lv_key.\\n        IF lv_key = iv_name.\\n          lv_from = lv_off + 1.\\n          rv_ = substring( val = lv_line off = lv_from ).\\n          CONDENSE rv_.\\n          EXIT.\\n        ENDIF.\\n      ENDDO.\\n      CLOSE DATASET iv_file.\\n    CATCH cx_root.\\n      CLEAR rv_.\\n  ENDTRY.\\nENDMETHOD.\\n```\\n\\nWait: there's a pre-existing bug: if OPEN DATASET fails, RETURN before CLOSE \u2014 fine. If READ fails... ok. Also CLOSE DATASET inside TRY; fine as-is.\\n\\nEdge: value containing '#' would be truncated \u2014 document with comment that '#' starts a comment per README.\\n\\nOne more: `CONDENSE rv_` on value: `glm-5.3 # optional` \u2192 after cut: `glm-5.3 ` \u2192 substring after '=' is ` glm-5.3 ` \u2192 condense \u2192 `glm-5.3`. Good.\\n\\nKey match case: `PIA_LLM = z.ai` \u2192 cleaned `PIA_LLM = z.ai` \u2192 key `PIA_LLM ` \u2192 condense \u2192 `PIA_LLM`. Match. Value ` z.ai` \u2192 condense \u2192 `z.ai`. Good.\\n\\nNow also check other code that reads pia.env \u2014 maybe other classes parse the file themselves (e.g., session store or LLM http reading PIA_API_KEY). The bug report mentions model and turn mode; those go through CONFIG. But let me check if any other class reads pia.env directly (grep-like). I can't grep; but maybe check ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP quickly for config usage. The report says the fix in CONFIG suffices. But if e.g. API key read elsewhere with same parsing... Let me check LLM_HTTP and EXECUTOR briefly for `OPEN DATASET` / pia.env usage. I'll read them after the fix to be safe (next turn). Actually, to be thorough, let me read ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP now in parallel with nothing... I already have the plan; I'll do: write main (public get_from, buggy) + write testclasses, activate. Then next turn run_tests. Also read LLM_HTTP to check for other pia.env readers in the same block as run? Reads are independent \u2014 I can batch read_object calls now.\\n\\nLet me proceed.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_202610072356491b90b338d7954af3\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"text\":\"The class has no test include yet. The environment's checker rejects `LOCAL FRIENDS` and private access here, so I'll make `GET_FROM` public (for ABAP Unit) with its still-buggy body, plus the test include \u2014 that gives me a compiling, red state.\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_202610072356491b90b338d7954af3\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"main\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS zcl_pia_00_config DEFINITION PUBLIC FINAL CREATE PUBLIC.\\\\n\\\\n  PUBLIC SECTION.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" NAME=value lines; never committed. OSG: dir in OSD_DATASET_READ / OSD_DATASET_HOME.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" SAP: application server file (DIR_HOME or full path).\\\\n    CONSTANTS c_file TYPE string VALUE `pia.env`.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" settings without secrets (PIA_LLM, PIA_MODEL, PIA_TURN_MODE); read when pia.env has no value\\\\n    CONSTANTS c_settings TYPE string VALUE `pia-settings.env`.\\\\n\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS get\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_name    TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    \\\\\\\" PIA_MODEL from pia.env, default glm-5.3 (glm-5.3-flash wrote invalid ABAP and empty tool args)\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS model\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    \\\\\\\" public only so the local ABAP Unit tests can inject their own file\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS get_from\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_file    TYPE string\\\\n                iv_name    TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS zcl_pia_00_config IMPLEMENTATION.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD model.\\\\n    rv_ = get( `PIA_MODEL` ).\\\\n    IF rv_ IS INITIAL.\\\\n      rv_ = `glm-5.3`.\\\\n    ENDIF.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD get.\\\\n    rv_ = get_from( iv_file = c_file iv_name = iv_name ).\\\\n    IF rv_ IS INITIAL.\\\\n      rv_ = get_from( iv_file = c_settings iv_name = iv_name ).\\\\n    ENDIF.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD get_from.\\\\n    DATA lv_line TYPE string.\\\\n    DATA lv_key TYPE string.\\\\n    DATA lv_off TYPE i.\\\\n    DATA lv_from TYPE i.\\\\n\\\\n    TRY.\\\\n        OPEN DATASET iv_file FOR INPUT IN TEXT MODE ENCODING UTF-8.\\\\n        IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\\\n          RETURN.\\\\n        ENDIF.\\\\n        DO.\\\\n          READ DATASET iv_file INTO lv_line.\\\\n          IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\\\n            EXIT.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n          CLEAR lv_off.\\\\n          FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF `=` IN lv_line MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\\\n          IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\\\n            CONTINUE.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n          lv_key = substring( val = lv_line len = lv_off ).\\\\n          IF lv_key = iv_name.\\\\n            lv_from = lv_off + 1.\\\\n            rv_ = substring( val = lv_line off = lv_from ).\\\\n            EXIT.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n        ENDDO.\\\\n        CLOSE DATASET iv_file.\\\\n      CATCH cx_root.\\\\n        CLEAR rv_.\\\\n    ENDTRY.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228032554434030173\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228032554434030173\",\"name\":\"write_source\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"main\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228032554434030172\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228032554434030172\",\"name\":\"read_object\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4382,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":3200},\"output_tokens\":3826,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":3145},\"total_tokens\":8208}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791388669,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_20261007235745bb6c1571d7484721\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: outline(name), read_method(name, method, class), write_method(name, method, source - one METHOD block, class), read_object(name, include main|testclasses), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: prefer outline, read_method and write_method for changing existing methods; use write_source only for new methods, changed declarations or a new test include, and then write the FULL source; read before write; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG (settings from pia.env), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The LLM client takes ms_config-model as-is. The fix belongs in CONFIG. Now activate the main include (get_from now public), then run tests (expected red), then fix GET_FROM.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_20261007235745bb6c1571d7484721\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228026953796680961\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-72280269537966809