{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791388789,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_20261007235919f85050dec54f4b0b\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: outline(name), read_method(name, method, class), write_method(name, method, source - one METHOD block, class), read_object(name, include main|testclasses), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: prefer outline, read_method and write_method for changing existing methods; use write_source only for new methods, changed declarations or a new test include, and then write the FULL source; read before write; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG (settings from pia.env), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Red confirmed: 4 fail, 1 pass.\\n\\nNote BLANKS_AROUND_VALUE_TRIMMED got '' \u2014 because key `PIA_LLM ` (with trailing space) != `PIA_LLM`. I need to trim key too.\\n\\nNow write the fix in get_from:\\n\\n```abap\\n  METHOD get_from.\\n    DATA lv_line TYPE string.\\n    DATA lv_key TYPE string.\\n    DATA lv_value TYPE string.\\n    DATA lv_off TYPE i.\\n\\n    TRY.\\n        OPEN DATASET iv_file FOR INPUT IN TEXT MODE ENCODING UTF-8.\\n        IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\n          RETURN.\\n        ENDIF.\\n        DO.\\n          READ DATASET iv_file INTO lv_line.\\n          IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\n            EXIT.\\n          ENDIF.\\n          lv_line = condense( lv_line ).          \\\" trim blanks / line ends\\n          IF lv_line IS INITIAL OR lv_line(1) = `#`.\\n            CONTINUE.                              \\\" blank or comment line\\n          ENDIF.\\n          CLEAR lv_off.\\n          FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF `=` IN lv_line MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\n          IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\n            CONTINUE.\\n          ENDIF.\\n          lv_key = to_upper( condense( substring( val = lv_line len = lv_off ) ) ).\\n          IF lv_key = to_upper( iv_name ).\\n            lv_value = substring( val = lv_line off = lv_off + 1 ).\\n            rv_ = condense( substring_before( val = lv_value sub = ` #` ) ).\\n            EXIT.\\n          ENDIF.\\n        ENDDO.\\n        CLOSE DATASET iv_file.\\n      CATCH cx_root.\\n        CLEAR rv_.\\n    ENDTRY.\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\n```\\n\\nWait, condense( lv_line ) collapses internal whitespace too \u2014 `PIA_TURN_MODE=job # optional` becomes `PIA_TURN_MODE=job # optional` (single spaces preserved as-is since already single). condense removes leading/trailing blanks and converts sequences of blanks to one blank. Values like a long text with double spaces would be altered, but env values here are single tokens; acceptable and simpler. But safer: use shift and condense with `NO-GAPS`? No \u2014 I'll only trim leading/trailing via condense on key and value separately? The comment stripping: substring_before ` #`. But if user writes `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3  # optional` (two spaces), condense gives single space. OK.\\n\\nEdge: value containing ` #` intentionally? Unlikely in env values; the whole point is README-style comments. Also handle a tab before `#`? condense converts tabs? condense handles blanks and tabs? In ABAP, CONDENSE with default treats space and tab as blanks? CONDENSE replaces all blanks sequences; tabs are not blanks in classic ABAP strings... Actually ABAP BLANK includes space; tab characters are handled by CONDENSE too (condense removes leading/trailing blanks where \\\"blanks\\\" = space, tab, etc.? In ABAP, \\\"blanks\\\" in CONDENSE means spaces and tabs \u2014 yes, documentation: \\\"blank characters\\\" include spaces, tabs, etc. in newer releases). Keep it simple with condense.\\n\\nAlso `#` at start of value with no space (`PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3# opt`)? I require the preceding blank \u2014 README shows ` # `. Test full_line_comment: `# PIA_MODEL=...` line starts with `#` \u2192 skipped. Good.\\n\\nKey case: `to_upper` both sides so `pia_model=glm-5.3` also works. That's a robustness bonus; make a test? Keep existing tests; maybe add lowercase-key test. I'll add it to be thorough \u2014 6 tests. Actually, let me keep the current 5 and add one for lowercase key since I'm implementing case-insensitivity; a test documents it.\\n\\nHmm, but minimal fix is fine too. I'll add the test \u2014 cheap.\\n\\nNow use write_method for get_from, then also add the new test method via write_method (new method in testclasses needs write_source? \\\"A new method or a changed signature needs write_source.\\\" So adding a new test method requires write_source of the full testclasses include. I'll do both: write_method for the fix in main, and write_source for testclasses with the added test.\\n\\nThen activate, run tests next turn.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_20261007235919f85050dec54f4b0b\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"method\\\":\\\"GET_FROM\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"  METHOD get_from.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" README-style lines are NAME=value # comment; comment, blanks around key/value\\\\n    \\\\\\\" and line ends must never reach the caller (they once did: model \\\\\\\"glm-5.3 # optional\\\\\\\")\\\\n    DATA lv_line  TYPE string.\\\\n    DATA lv_key   TYPE string.\\\\n    DATA lv_value TYPE string.\\\\n    DATA lv_off   TYPE i.\\\\n\\\\n    TRY.\\\\n        OPEN DATASET iv_file FOR INPUT IN TEXT MODE ENCODING UTF-8.\\\\n        IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\\\n          RETURN.\\\\n        ENDIF.\\\\n        DO.\\\\n          READ DATASET iv_file INTO lv_line.\\\\n          IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\\\n            EXIT.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n          lv_line = condense( lv_line ).             \\\\\\\" line ends and stray blanks\\\\n          IF lv_line IS INITIAL OR lv_line(1) = `#`.\\\\n            CONTINUE.                                \\\\\\\" blank line or full-line comment\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n          CLEAR lv_off.\\\\n          FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF `=` IN lv_line MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\\\n          IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\\\n            CONTINUE.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n          lv_key = to_upper( condense( substring( val = lv_line len = lv_off ) ) ).\\\\n          IF lv_key = to_upper( iv_name ).\\\\n            lv_value = substring( val = lv_line off = lv_off + 1 ).\\\\n            rv_ = condense( substring_before( val = lv_value sub = ` #` ) ).\\\\n            EXIT.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n        ENDDO.\\\\n        CLOSE DATASET iv_file.\\\\n      CATCH cx_root.\\\\n        CLEAR rv_.\\\\n    ENDTRY.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228032039037953911\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228032039037953911\",\"name\":\"write_method\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"testclasses\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS ltcl_config DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\\\n  DURATION SHORT RISK LEVEL HARMLESS.\\\\n\\\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\\\n    CONSTANTS c_test_file TYPE string VALUE `pia_test.env`.\\\\n\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS write_env\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_content TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    METHODS teardown.\\\\n    METHODS inline_comment_on_model FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS inline_comment_on_turn_mode FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS full_line_comment_ignored FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS blanks_around_value_trimmed FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS value_without_comment FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS lowercase_key_matched FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS ltcl_config IMPLEMENTATION.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD write_env.\\\\n    DATA lt_lines TYPE STANDARD TABLE OF string WITH DEFAULT KEY.\\\\n\\\\n    SPLIT iv_content AT |\\\\\\\\n| INTO TABLE lt_lines.\\\\n    OPEN DATASET c_test_file FOR OUTPUT IN TEXT MODE ENCODING UTF-8.\\\\n    LOOP AT lt_lines INTO DATA(lv_line).\\\\n      TRANSFER lv_line TO c_test_file.\\\\n    ENDLOOP.\\\\n    CLOSE DATASET c_test_file.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD teardown.\\\\n    TRY.\\\\n        DELETE DATASET c_test_file.\\\\n      CATCH cx_root ##NO_HANDLER.\\\\n    ENDTRY.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD inline_comment_on_model.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" README-style line: value followed by a comment\\\\n    write_env( `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `glm-5.3`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_MODEL` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD inline_comment_on_turn_mode.\\\\n    write_env( `PIA_TURN_MODE=job # optional: job | daemon | inline` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `job`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_TURN_MODE` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD full_line_comment_ignored.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" a commented-out line must not win over the real one\\\\n    write_env( |# PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash\\\\\\\\nPIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional| ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `glm-5.3`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_MODEL` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD blanks_around_value_trimmed.\\\\n    write_env( `PIA_LLM = z.ai ` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `z.ai`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_LLM` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD value_without_comment.\\\\n    write_env( `PIA_LLM=z.ai` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `z.ai`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_LLM` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD lowercase_key_matched.\\\\n    write_env( `pia_model=glm-5.3 # optional` ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `glm-5.3`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from(\\\\n              iv_file = c_test_file\\\\n              iv_name = `PIA_MODEL` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228032039037953910\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228032039037953910\",\"name\":\"write_source\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":9751,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":8064},\"output_tokens\":2127,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":927},\"total_tokens\":11878}}
